# Normalize line endings. Shell scripts MUST stay LF or they break on Linux
# (a CRLF shebang yields "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M").
* text=auto
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
# Settings-drift fixtures are byte-exact input: `* text=auto` would rewrite line
# endings and could turn the CRLF/empty/whitespace cases into different tests.
# -text pins every fixture file as-is, so the committed blob of crlf-live/live.json
# holds real CR bytes and is CRLF on every checkout (an eol=crlf rule would store it
# normalised and leave Linux checkouts with a plain-LF "CRLF" test).
/scripts/settings-drift-fixtures/** -text
# ...except the contract README: it is prose, not input, and should follow the
# normal Markdown line-ending handling like every other .md file.
/scripts/settings-drift-fixtures/README.md text=auto
